00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.720
Or find me on LinkedIn and
send me your email address.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.170
That way also works.
Thank you, Rachel.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.210
- Yeah, absolutely. And ISLR,

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:27.870
that's Introduction
to Statistical Learning--

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.960
- Introduction to Statistical Learning
in R, yes. Thank you.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.550
Sorry-- all the acronyms.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.730
- No, no. worries. Awesome.
That sounds great. Yeah,

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.820
feel free to put that
into the chat, of course,

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:42.060
to let people know who
are joining in later too.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:46.840
But with that, Brian, thank you
so much for joining us today.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.330
So Brian is our--

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.750
Brian Fannin is our featured
leader for the day and he's

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.590
